  "profile_long": "The provided sources contain no information regarding the dance tradition known as Rapo. The sources are exclusively biographical documents concerning Sreeleela, an American-born actress of Indian origin who works primarily in Telugu and Kannada cinema. According to the sources, Sreeleela was born on June 14, 2001, in Detroit, Michigan, and raised in Bengaluru, India. She began her training in the classical Indian dance form Bharatanatyam during her childhood. In 2026, she completed an MBBS degree from the D. Y. Patil School of Medicine in Navi Mumbai. Her career in cinema began with the 2019 Kannada film Kiss, followed by roles in films such as Pelli SandaD, Dhamaka, and Bhagavanth Kesari. The sources provide extensive detail on her filmography, awards, and personal life, including her adoption of disabled children, but do not mention any dance tradition called Rapo.",
